<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sadras</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sadurangapattinam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sadras, now Sadurangapattinam, is a coastal village south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Chennai</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. In the 17th century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> built a fortified trading post there to buy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> textiles woven in the area. The remains of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fort, with its warehouses and cemetery, are a protected monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sadras.jpg" alt="Sadras" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shadows Galore from Chennai, India · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sadras_fort2_cannon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
